+
+## Findings
+
+**Klintvägen's bend is a 1978 addition.** In 1968 Klintvägen runs straight south and continues as today's Klintgränd. The south-west bend to Västra Utfarten is first drawn in 1978, in the same thick red overprint as the other new roads of that revision. Klintvägen is therefore a partial extent in 1968–1977: a substring of the modern line ending at the Klintgränd junction. The whole street is shown from 1978. Its connection to Västra Utfarten (two lanes and the short crossing pieces) starts in 1978. Klintgränd keeps 1968. The second pass deferred this bend; it is now dated.
+
+**Västra Utfarten's west carriageway is drawn only from 1995.** In 1968–1985 the maps draw one red road. The modern west carriageway lies 6–9 m from the dated east one, inside that symbol, so those editions are recorded as *unclear*. In 1995 the map shows two carriageways. The lane starts then and counts 0 m. Framnäsvägen and Varvsvägen, which are streets by 1985, join this carriageway. Dated from 1985, they would end 6–9 m short of the network for ten years, so they stay deferred.
+
+**Single lines and thin overprint are not streets.** In 1968 Bagargränd, Murargränd, Formansgränd and Gjutargränd are single solid lines between rows of houses, while the streets around them are double-lined. Those editions are recorded as *unclear*, and the gränder start in 1985. As in the third pass, thin red 1978 lines along later Ytternäs streets and Vikingagränd are *unclear*. Black lines in 1995 (Lekgränd, Gnistvägen, the Kas-, Å- and Vikbrinken lanes) are left for the road-to-path model.
+
+**The 1995 Stenliden block is deferred, not dated.** Uppgårdsvägen, Östra Stenliden, Kråkbärsstigen, Blåbärsstigen and Hjortronstigen are first drawn as red streets in 1995. The northernmost part of Uppgårdsvägen (way 88561577) is not a street even then. Today the block reaches the dated network only through undated Nya Godbyvägen junction pieces, Doktorsvägen's service section and cycleways. Bergshöjden (a street from 1985) ends without a modern junction at either end. All of these wait until those junctions are reviewed.
+
+## Method and data
+
+Same method as the third pass, with contact sheets in `data/map-scan-cache/review/mariehamn-major-roads/pass4/` (`waysheet.py`, `crop.py`). Area crops `klint-*`, `klintbend-*`, `sten-*` and `vik-*` were used where a sheet was not decisive. `data/mariehamn-street-pass4.json` is generated by `pass4/prepare.py` against the snapshot `pass4/before.json.gz`, which is identical to the published catalogue after the third pass. Keep the script for audit; do not rerun it blindly. `scripts/mariehamn_street_pass4.py` runs after the third pass with the shared `apply_reviewed_streets` (marker `mariehamnStreetPass4`). The shared validator already handles partial extents, `longest` lanes and `parallel` lanes, so it is unchanged.
+
+## Deferred
+
+These are listed in the review file and stay undated:
+
+- The Stenliden block and Bergshöjden (see Findings). Framnäsvägen and Varvsvägen, until Västra Utfarten's carriageway can be dated earlier or the junction is reviewed.
+- Mästargränd and Ekogränd: the 1968 loop does not follow today's Ekogränd, and Mästargränd's eastern connection is a footway today.
+- Knipgränd, Alfågelgränd and Tibastvägen (streets by 1985), which connect only through Skrakvägen and Roskarlsvägen outside the city base, or through cycleways.
+- Streets that are not red in 1995: Skönviksvägen, Nybondas, Snickerivägen, Sylgränd, Slantgränd. The black 1995 lines listed above.
+- Unclear position, extent or connection: Bergsvägen, Tvärgränd, Hasselstigen, Kvarngränd, Kilvägen, Lagervägen, Strandgränd, Algotsgränd, Björkvägen, Hagtornsvägen, Kottstigen, Syrengränd, Michaelsvägen. Old roads on another line than today's street (Servicegatan's southern part, Villagränd, Bäckvägen, Nybondasvägen) need a realignment review.
+- Absent up to 1995: Fågelberget (Fågellänken, Vråkvägen, Hökvägen and their neighbours), Blomstringevägen, Skrapängsvägen, Juseliusvägen, Palettgränd, Akvarellgränd, Pastellgränd. The streets west of Möckelö lie off sheet 101208.
+
+## Validation
+
+`pass4/audit.py` rebuilds the catalogue with the pass disabled and confirms that the baseline equals the snapshot. Against it, the pass adds 63 objects (36,126 → 36,189), 389 geometries (46,450 → 46,839), all with the pass's prefix, and one source. No existing object, geometry or city stage changes, and no source feature gains a second owner (`pass4/scope-audit.json`).
+
+`tests/mariehamn-street-pass4.test.cjs` checks:
+
+- the totals by first edition, with the parallel lane at 0 m and the Klintvägen lanes counted once;
+- each start against the observations, with stable geometry to 2026 and one city-stage feature per stage;
+- single ownership against all earlier passes, and that deferred ways stay unowned;
+- the partial extents of Klintvägen and Mjölnargränd;
+- that every street joins a road drawn in its first edition (this check moved the Stenliden block, Bergshöjden, Mästargränd, Knipgränd, Alfågelgränd and Tibastvägen to the deferred list);
+- the dating rules for single 1968 lines, thin 1978 overprint and the west carriageway.
+
+`tests/test_mariehamn_street_pass4.py` checks:
+
+- that the review applies once and matches the build;
+- that it needs the third pass;
+- that it rejects early starts, wrong partial extents, double ownership, discontinuous sections, changed inputs, wrong lengths, a counted parallel lane, a lane counted as display, and a lane present while only one road is drawn.
+
+`tests/temporal-objects.test.cjs` counts the new identities. The loader's recent-changes note has a new first card.
+
+**Publication.** Deployed 2026-11-12 as Cloudflare version `e9000b11-534f-4a4e-b00a-8a86403cec36`. The release was prepared from the live version (`167275da…`) plus only this pass: the catalogue, `assets/mariehamn-street-pass4.json`, the loader card in `index.html`, and cache stamps in `temporal-objects.js` and `object.html`. Other unpublished workspace changes were left out. Of the 137 relevant JavaScript tests run against the release tree, all passed. All 287 live files were checked byte for byte against the release; see `pass4/deployment.json`.
